<http://data.silknow.org/object/ef01d343-0bde-3918-9007-9c2bd59d171d>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "embroidered, 1800s, Persian; Whitework"@en , "Plain weave linen? or cotton, probably handwoven, embroidered with silk in straight stitches and pulled thread work; whitework.\nTop and bottom edges have been rolled and stitched in place. The central panel is decorated with a large lozenge form composed of 4 lozenges with 3 different patterns, with a variety of pulled thread and straight stitch forms, irregular in motif and scale.  This is edged with 2 narrow lines of pulled thread work with a narrow diagonal band in between.  The remaining triangular corner units are filled with a regular pulled thread net-like pattern. This band is surrounded by a band of linking lozenge forms, composed of either 8 triangles of straight stitch or the pulled thread net patterning of the corner units.\nLinen or Cotton Thread: white, Z-spun, tightly spun\nEmbroidery Thread: white silk; 2S"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/d0cc27fd-05ed-3496-8ae6-b67f5f21d95e> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Plain weave linen? or cotton, probably handwoven, embroidered with silk in straight stitches and pulled thread work; whitework.\nTop and bottom edges have been rolled and stitched in place. The central panel is decorated with a large lozenge form composed of 4 lozenges with 3 different patterns, with a variety of pulled thread and straight stitch forms, irregular in motif and scale.  This is edged with 2 narrow lines of pulled thread work with a narrow diagonal band in between.  The remaining triangular corner units are filled with a regular pulled thread net-like pattern. This band is surrounded by a band of linking lozenge forms, composed of either 8 triangles of straight stitch or the pulled thread net patterning of the corner units.\nLinen or Cotton Thread: white, Z-spun, tightly spun\nEmbroidery Thread: white silk; 2S"@en , "embroidered, 1800s, Persian; Whitework"@en ;
